==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|LL.|theophania}}, corresponding to {{af|en|theo-|-phany}}, from {{m|grc|θεο||God}} + {{m|grc|φαίνω||I shine, appear}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/θiːˈɒfəni/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A manifestation of a [[deity]] to a person.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2009|author={{w|Karen Armstrong}}|title=The Case for God|page=47|publisher=Vintage|year_published=2010
|passage=It was a bewildering '''theophany''', since it was impossible to make out anything clearly in the stormy obscurity of thunder, lightning, smoke and wind.}}

